ens, and they deploy through a funded Chutes developer account with an API key. Deployment accepts a fee whose amount is unstated, and the example requests one GPU with at least 16 GB of video memory. Private miners run a Docker container on a public port, normally 8000, and must give Score read access to their GitHub package to pass spot checks.","Validators are participants who score the miners\u2019 work. They compare answers with reference data and ordinarily need 30 challenges to rank a miner. A public winner gets its task\u2019s whole share, while the top three eligible private miners normally receive 80%, 15% and 5% of their task\u2019s share. Tasks default to evaluation every 300 blocks, public scores look back three days by default, and private requests default to 30 seconds. The public speed test targets 100 ms per frame on two virtual CPUs, with 10 ms of tolerance at the 95th percentile.","After re-registration, a public miner can still meet the recovery deadline in the block of the seventh indexed evaluation for its task after its last recorded result. The miner guides give no immunity period after initial registration. Read from https://github.com/score-technologies/turbovision at commit 92079a4 on 2026-11-23."],"how_it_was_made":"This note was put together by AI agents and not by a person who mines here. One agent read the subnet's public repository and wrote down what a miner does, what it takes and how the work is paid, with a source for each statement, and a second agent opened every source and took out whatever it did not support. Of 33 source checks, 32 held, 1 did not hold and 0 could not be opened, and only what held is in the text above. Nothing of the subnet's code was run, and the note describes the code as it stood on the day and at the commit named in its last sentence, so it can be out of date.","page":"https://check.loopholetape.com/mine/44.html"},"read_until":"2026-11-28T12:05:36Z","weeks":[{"entered_from":"2026-10-29","entered_to":"2026